# TestJavaToCSharpTimefold: timefold-solver's core/main translated to C# and judged by Roslyn (JavaToCSharpRatchet).
# Lower is better for printerCrashes, syntaxErrors and unmappedJdkUses, higher for syntaxCleanFiles and
# compilingFiles; `types` must not move. Write a better value here in the commit that earns it.
#
# 2026-10-12, first record: 611 of 1583 files compile, 8744 errors. Most are generics: CS0311 (a type argument that
# does not satisfy a constraint: an F-bounded type's wildcard, Score<?>, printed as IScore<IScore<object>>) and
# CS0411 (type inference). 21 syntax errors: OptionalInt's statics (int?.empty()) and a cast of a method reference
# printed as a lambda. maddi-mod's timefold-facts ratchet measures the same with the analysis's facts.
#
# 2026-10-12, OptionalInt's of and empty ((int?) x, (int?) null) and a method reference in parentheses as an operand:
# 21 -> 0 syntax errors, 611 -> 615 compiling files (8879 errors: the 4 syntax-clean files now compile further).
#
# 2026-10-12, the type arguments Java infers and C# cannot (a method type parameter no parameter mentions, Value_
# getStore(int)) printed explicitly: 615 -> 656 compiling files, 8879 -> 8236 errors (CS0411 1101 -> 414).
#
# 2026-10-12, inner classes take their enclosing instance (CSharpInner: the field outer, constructors that take it,
# outer.member): CS0120 412 -> 1, 656 -> 696 compiling files, 8236 -> 7848 errors.
#
# 2026-10-12, an interface's method left abstract is declared once, by the first abstract class (a second hid it:
# CS0533, and the subclasses' overrides missed it: CS0534 393 -> 215); field initializers that use this run in the
# constructor (CS0027): 696 -> 725 compiling files, 7848 -> 7578 errors.
#
# 2026-10-12, mappings: RandomGenerator (Random), BigDecimal's constants and the rest of its arithmetic, BigInteger's,
# RoundingMode (MidpointRounding), the To*Function delegates, getCanonicalName, emptyIterator, newHashMap(n), …; a
# supplier with a block body called through its delegate in a template: 2082 -> 1379 unmapped JDK uses, 725 -> 777
# compiling files.
#
# 2026-10-12, a switch on an enum printed as a class matches the instances' Name, { Name: "FAST" } (CS9135 202 -> 0),
# and falls through into such a section by a statement label: 777 -> 787 compiling files, 6951 -> 6751 errors.
#
# 2026-10-12, companions of self-bounded types (CSharpCompanions: IScore beside IScore<Score_>) for their wildcards
# and raw uses: CS0311 2198 -> 76, 787 -> 827 compiling files, 6751 -> 4586 errors.
#
# 2026-10-12, the logging mapping's using for its extension methods, a diamond's arguments from its constructor's
# arguments, Iterable interfaces enumerable by default implementations: 827 -> 833 compiling files, 4586 -> 4302
# errors.
#
# 2026-10-12, a generic method overridden by erasure printed erased (CS0534 215 -> 130); a raw array passed as a
# variable arity parameter's array gets the parameter's type arguments, new IBiJoiner<A, B>[] { joiner }: 833 -> 837
# compiling files, 4302 -> 3594 errors.
#
# 2026-10-12, a self-bounded type parameter only a result mentions (<Score_ extends Score<Score_>> InnerScore<Score_>
# getScore()) printed erased, its result the companion; records get companions; a companion of a Comparable<Score_>
# is IComparable; T of a Class<T> argument inferred from the wildcard's bound: CS0411 398 -> 152, CS0311 76 -> 41,
# 837 -> 868 compiling files, 3594 -> 3304 errors. unmappedJdkUses 1379 -> 1380: NewInstance<ThreadFactory> now
# names the unmapped ThreadFactory as a type argument.
#
# 2026-10-12, a diamond argument gets the type Java inferred for its parameter (share(new Bridge<>(…), g::setBridge));
# a delegate variable where Java's wildcard or raw type is expected is wrapped, x0_ => f(x0_), for C#'s variance:
# CS1503 347 -> 256, CS0246 539 -> 494, 3304 -> 3168 errors, 868 compiling files (the files have other errors too).
# unmappedJdkUses 1380 -> 1386: the lambdas' parameter casts name types already unmapped (gizmo's Expr, BlockCreator,
# java.net.URL).
#
# 2026-10-12, the bases of a public type are public (Java's public class may extend a package-private one): CS0060
# 73 -> 1, 868 -> 925 compiling files, 3168 -> 3095 errors.
#
# 2026-10-12, in a type's own instance members a cast to or a local of its wildcard is the type itself (Java's equals
# reads the other instance's private fields, which the companion has not): CS1061 371 -> 325, 925 -> 945 compiling
# files, 3095 -> 3050 errors.
#
# 2026-10-12, an abstract redeclaration checked against every ancestor (CS0533 16 -> 0, CS0534 130 -> 109), a method
# group's type arguments only its result gives (AbstractMinMaxSlot.MinState<Result_>), Slot::new of an inner class with
# its enclosing instance (CS7036 60 -> 38): 945 -> 986 compiling files, 3050 -> 2981 errors.
#
# 2026-10-12, an override repeats no constraints (CS0460 83 -> 0); a raw constructor reference creates the type Java
# inferred for its result, Triple::new as new Triple<A, B, C>(…), HashSet::new as new HashSet<V>(…) (CS0029 224 -> 193,
# CS1662 55 -> 30): 986 -> 1013 compiling files, 2981 -> 2834 errors.
#
# 2026-10-12, without Gizmo (timefold-gizmo.csmap): Quarkus's bytecode generation has no .NET counterpart, its 18 types
